#
# Compositor: an animation that is off the surface is ticked at 10 Hz.
#
# ThreadedCompositor recomposited every frame while any layer had a running
# animation, visible or not. Wikipedia's mobile pages carry an infinite CSS
# "pulsating dot" on a header button: scrolled out of view, it kept an idle
# page compositing ~95 frames a second on the Jolla Phone (measured).
#
# SkiaCompositingLayer notes, while it computes the transforms each paint,
# whether a layer with a running animation touches the surface (a sizeless
# animated container counts as visible, since its children move with it).
# After three animation-only frames with none on the surface, the next
# animation frame waits 100 ms; one coming into view, or any other reason to
# composite, returns to full rate. (Damage tracking would be the general
# answer, but needs ENABLE(WPE_PLATFORM).) PACIFIC_DEBUG_ANIMATIONS=1 logs
# each animation frame's verdict.
#
